message: "If you use these results or code, please cite them as below."
title: "Erdős Problem #757: no (4,5)-set with Sidon ratio below 4/7 on fewer than 25 points, and the 14-point classification"
abstract: >-
  Computer-assisted results on Erdős Problem #757 (Tao's constant C_5b). Using the
  3-AP hypergraph reduction of Ma and Tang (arXiv 2602.23282), exhaustive isomorph-free
  enumerations of linear 3-graphs and an exact rank test for realisability, no
  (4,5)-set has n = 16, h <= 9; n = 18, h <= 10; n = 20, h <= 11; n = 22, h <= 12; or
  n = 23, h <= 13. By the Henning–Yeo transversal bound these are the only shapes with
  n <= 24 below 4/7, so every (4,5)-set with Sidon ratio below 4/7 has at least 25
  points (n = 16, 18, 20 are Henning–Yeo-free). Every 14-point (4,5)-set with h = 8 has
  exactly 12 three-term progressions and one of 9 progression-hypergraph types.
